# Osseous Sticktwister in a three-player game: turn 1 as in its first scenario (the Wheel of Fortune gives Bot1 four card
# types). At Bot1's end step the opponents choose in turn order (CR 101.4), Bot2 first; Bot3 concedes while Bot2 is still
# choosing which card to discard (CR 104.3a), so when the choosing comes round to Bot3 it has left the game and is asked
# nothing (CR 800.4a). Bot2 discarded, so no one takes damage and there is no lifelink gain: both stay at 20.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Osseous Sticktwister
Wheel of Fortune
Memnite
Island
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x40

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x40

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Osseous Sticktwister.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Wheel of Fortune.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Modes(Discard a card)
Bot3.Concede
Bot2.Choose(Island)
? Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
? Bot2.Life = 20
? Bot1.Life = 20

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
Bot3.Status = Lost
